    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer the driver to driver-conduct review — a MATERIAL, substantiated deviation on trip TRP-00515 combined with an established repeat-deviation pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3) requires conduct review, and this referral rides with the monetary ruling without delaying it."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This is one trip, TRP-00515, and it is decided on clean evidence. The GPS trace covers 100% of the trip at a 10-second cadence, with no gaps (max_gap_sec 0.0) and no jumps, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) and nothing on it is discounted. On that trace the car covered 48.82 km against the booked optimal of 34.2 km — an excess of 14.62 km, which is 42.75% of optimal and clears both POL-RD-01 gates (20% and 0.8 km). The excess also exceeds the 8.0 km absolute figure, so the deviation is MATERIAL. The trip record's 48.8 km figure is a rounded copy and was not used for the threshold test.\n\nThe refund arithmetic, run as POL-RD-02 requires on this METERED fare, is: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 × 34.2 km + 0.28 × 40.0 min) × surge 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 on-optimal-route ERP = 41.45. Against charged_total of 62.28 that is 20.83, rounded up to a payable 20.85. That is the figure the driver's advocate put forward, and it is right as far as it goes — but only as the POL-RD-02 partial.\n\nPOL-RD-06 does more here. The deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own evidence (the 14.62 km trace excess, the two off-optimal ERP gantries, and the driver's own filed admission that he missed the KPE split). The driver's profile shows deviation_flags_90d = 3, which meets POL-RD-06's pattern test ('3 or more'), so the pattern is established and limb (b) applies. That limb licenses FULL_REFUND of the charged total in place of the POL-RD-02 partial. The two figures side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 figure 20.85; uplifted figure 62.28. The rider recovers 62.28.\n\nThe 4.00 of ERP (two TPE gantries at 2.00 each, both recorded on_optimal_route = false) is government/third-party pass-through, settled under POL-RD-09 and not uplifted. Under POL-RD-09(1) it is already comprehended in the refund and is never added on top; both gantries were genuinely crossed (nearest trace fix 0.0 m to each), so there is no phantom line and no billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4). The ERP portion is refunded at face value within the total, not doubled.\n\nNo exculpatory clause rescues the driver. The only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00515-01, is MISSING — no payload, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the driver does not contest that. The single chat message carries waypoint_hint null and names no place or road, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test is undecidable and the clause is unavailable. No endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-05 has nothing to re-quote, and the vehicle is RYDE_PLUS, not a pooled trip, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply and 34.2 km is the correct baseline. The driver's assertion that the extra distance 'wasn't that much' cites no evidence and carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The missing advisory is not relied on by this ruling, so it does not cap confidence (POL-GEN-02(2)).\n\nOn the rider's account: the elapsed time was 61 minutes, not the 90 asserted, so that part of the narrative is overstated, and the money does not turn on the phone-use allegations — but the deviation finding rests on the trace, not on the narrative. POL-RD-06(c) requires a referral to driver-conduct review, and that referral is recorded above; it is an addition to the money, not a substitute for it. Confidence is 0.9, consistent with the deciding artifacts (trace, fare ledger, trip record, driver profile) all carrying full weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 62.28,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer driver DRV-21377 to driver-conduct review — this trip's MATERIAL deviation (14.62 km excess, 42.75% over the 34.2 km optimal) meets the POL-RD-06 pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3), and the rider's in-app message at 17:48:40 ('can you please put the phone down and drive') together with the driver's own statement that he was checking navigation on his phone supports it. The referral rides with the monetary ruling and does not displace or delay it."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This was one trip, TRP-00515, Jurong East to Punggol Dr, and the GPS trace is clean: 100% coverage at a 10-second cadence, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0. Nothing in the trace is impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07, and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires — the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, the timestamps are consistent, every fare line has a counterpart, and the refund is well under SGD 150.\n\nFINDING — the deviation is established. The governing distance is the trace figure, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 48.82 km. POL-RD-01 forbids citing the trip record's rounded 48.8 km, so I use 48.82. Against the booked optimal of 34.2 km that is an excess of 14.62 km, which is 42.75% of optimal (past the 20% gate) and far past the 0.8 km absolute gate — both tests pass, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. Because 14.62 km also exceeds 8.0 km, it is a MATERIAL deviation and the driver_profile check in POL-RD-06 is engaged.\n\nNo exculpatory clause runs. There is no traffic advisory in the pool: EV-ADVIS-00515-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run. The only chat message (rider, 17:48:40, 'can you please put the phone down and drive') carries waypoint_hint null and names no place or road, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test is undecidable on the record, the clause is unavailable, and I say so as POL-RD-04 requires. The trip was not pooled (vehicle_type RYDE_PLUS, not RYDE_POOL) and no endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply; and the fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the refund route.\n\nQUANTUM — the POL-RD-02 figure, and why the rider gets more. On POL-RD-02 arithmetic alone: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 34.2 km + 0.28 x 40.0 min) x surge 1.0 (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 optimal-route ERP = SGD 41.45; refund = 62.28 - 41.45 = SGD 20.83, rounded up to SGD 20.85. That is the figure the driver advocate asks for, and the driver is right that SGD 20.83 is 33.4% of the SGD 62.28 charged, far below the 90% share that would convert a partial into a full refund under POL-RD-02. But POL-RD-06(b) displaces that arithmetic here. The deviation is MATERIAL and it is substantiated on this trip's own evidence (the unimpaired trace, 14.62 km of excess), and the pattern is established because driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3, which is '3 or more' on the trailing-90-day counter POL-RD-06 actually names. I do not use prior_deviation_flags = 5; it is a lifetime counter and POL-GEN-01 makes it context only — only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d may carry a POL-RD-06 finding, and the rider's own claim disclaims the lifetime figure. POL-RD-06(b) therefore licenses FULL_REFUND of charged_total instead of the POL-RD-02 partial. Stated side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 figure SGD 20.85; uplifted figure SGD 62.28.\n\nThe government-set pass-through lines are not uplifted. The SGD 4.00 of ERP (two gantries, SGD 2.00 each, TPE Seletar Link and TPE Punggol Rd, both on_optimal_route false) is settled under POL-RD-09 and itemised for transparency; it forms part of the SGD 62.28 and is never added on top of it. Both gantries are real crossings — the nearest trace fix to each is 0.0 m — so there is no phantom line and no billing-integrity finding under POL-RD-09(4), and no billing-integrity referral. The off-route ERP is simply comprehended in the refund.\n\nClaim not accepted. The driver's submission that the extra distance 'wasn't that much' cites no evidence ID at all and carries no weight on POL-RD-08; the trace measures it at 14.62 km. The driver's related point that the POL-RD-06(b) uplift should leave the SGD 4.00 of ERP out of the uplift is correct as far as it goes, and is applied above — but it does not collapse the uplift back to the SGD 20.85 partial. The rider's dangerous-driving narrative is colour, not money: the fare lines do not move on it, and the ride ran 61 minutes end to end, not the 90 asserted. The rider's request for the whole contested amount succeeds, but on POL-RD-06(b) and the fare arithmetic, not on the conduct account.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The deciding facts rest on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00515, weight 1.0), the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00515, weight 1.0) and the driver profile (EV-DPROF-00515, weight 1.0), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and I set confidence at 0.9. The absent advisory carries no fact and does not drag the ruling."
  },
